      "text": "The given points are $\\left(\\frac{t+1}{t}, \\frac{t-1}{t}\\right)$. To find the common locus, we follow these steps:\n\n1. Set up the ratio of $x$ to $y$ to find a relationship between them:\n   \\[x = \\frac{t+1}{t}, \\quad y = \\frac{t-1}{t}.\\]\n\n2. Simplify the equations by dividing each by $t$ (since $t \\neq 0$):\n   \\[x = 1 + \\frac{1}{t}, \\quad y = 1 - \\frac{1}{t}.\\]\n\n3. Rearrange the equations to find a direct relationship between $x$ and $y$:\n   \\[x - 1 = \\frac{1}{t}, \\quad y - 1 = -\\frac{1}{t} \\implies x - 1 = -\\left(y - 1\\right).\\]\n\n4. Thus, the points $(x, y)$ satisfy the equation $x - 1 = -y + 1$ or equivalently $x + y = 2$. This represents a straight line in the xy-plane.\n\nTherefore, all the plotted points lie on a $\\boxed{\\text{A. Line}}$.",
